    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Find, using the Pythagorean identity:\n$$\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sin^3 x\\,dx$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac5{24}$",
      "worked": "$$\\sin^3 x=\\sin x(1-\\cos^2 x)$$\n$$\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sin^3 x\\,dx=\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sin x(1-\\cos^2 x)\\,dx$$\nLet $u=\\cos x$, so $du=-\\sin x\\,dx$.\n\nThe limits become $u=1$ when $x=0$, and $u=\\frac12$ when $x=\\frac\\pi3$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sin^3 x\\,dx&=-\\int_1^{1/2}(1-u^2)\\,du\\\\&=\\int_{1/2}^1(1-u^2)\\,du\\\\&=\\left[u-\\frac{u^3}{3}\\right]_{1/2}^1\\\\&=\\left(1-\\frac13\\right)-\\left(\\frac12-\\frac1{24}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac5{24}.\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
